id: pm-github-cited-issue-adoption
title: Require opt-in before adopting cited GitHub issue items
description: "Keep normal import creates and structured identity matching by default while reporting read-only citation candidates. Require explicit opt-in, bounded text normalization and anchored ownership checks before reusing a cited item. Document provenance tags at item creation as primary prevention, and validate encoded references, no-git persistence, workflow propagation and public dry runs."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: changelog-unreleased,github,import
created_at: "2026-10-23T07:16:54.041Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T21:53:34.315Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-24T21:53:34.304Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-24T21:53:34.304Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Adoption is off by default across CLI, SDK and reusable sync, enabled only with --adopt-cited, adoptCited true or adopt-cited true respectively. Default import retains normal create/structured-match behavior and read-only citation_candidates without fallback ambiguity refusal. Document creating items with gh:owner/repo#N as primary duplicate prevention; Normalize HTML named/numeric entities and percent bytes repeatedly until stable with a bounded refusal, apply NFKC and remove invisible/bidi controls, unwrap Markdown links/reference definitions and join soft breaks before anchored ownership checks while retaining source for conservative exclusion; Only title qualified references, leading description closing-keyword references, or whole body Issue:/Tracks: URL lines can authorize opt-in adoption. Any other normalized GitHub URL, foreign repository, other number or unattributed reference refuses adoption and reports candidate hints. Preserve structured identity precedence, single-owner upsert, eligible-owner ambiguity refusal, receipts, idempotency and non-git support; Keep all review reproductions and prior shape inputs, add encoded-reference fuzzing and explicit pm-review Issue label positives/default creates, record behavioral function/workflow reverts and public dry-run receipts, run targeted checks and wait for exact-head npm/Bun CI release gates"
resolution: "Citation adoption is explicit opt-in across CLI/SDK/workflow; bounded normalization and anchored ownership checks retain ambiguity refusals, structured identity and no-git idempotency."
expected_result: "Adoption is off by default across CLI, SDK and reusable sync, enabled only with --adopt-cited, adoptCited true or adopt-cited true respectively. Default import retains normal create/structured-match behavior and read-only citation_candidates without fallback ambiguity refusal. Document creating items with gh:owner/repo#N as primary duplicate prevention; Normalize HTML named/numeric entities and percent bytes repeatedly until stable with a bounded refusal, apply NFKC and remove invisible/bidi controls, unwrap Markdown links/reference definitions and join soft breaks before anchored ownership checks while retaining source for conservative exclusion; Only title qualified references, leading description closing-keyword references, or whole body Issue:/Tracks: URL lines can authorize opt-in adoption. Any other normalized GitHub URL, foreign repository, other number or unattributed reference refuses adoption and reports candidate hints. Preserve structured identity precedence, single-owner upsert, eligible-owner ambiguity refusal, receipts, idempotency and non-git support; Keep all review reproductions and prior shape inputs, add encoded-reference fuzzing and explicit pm-review Issue label positives/default creates, record behavioral function/workflow reverts and public dry-run receipts, run targeted checks and wait for exact-head npm/Bun CI release gates"
actual_result: "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/169, merged 2026-10-23T17:16:37Z, merge 1fec9f3968d2cf5f8564f1e2ce7c29f41979d947: Citation adoption is explicit opt-in across CLI/SDK/workflow; bounded normalization and anchored ownership checks retain ambiguity refusals, structured identity and no-git idempotency."
comments[48]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T07:17:26.861Z",codex-agent,"Overlap review: pm-github-c093 owns structured URL/provider back-link import matching, pm-github-identity-collisions diagnoses and repairs structured ownership, Projects import matches board and issue provenance, and export upserts linked issues. None adopts arbitrary exact prose citations. This feature adds a fallback only after existing import matching, preserving those paths. Scheduled gated sync already invokes import, so it inherits the default. Plan ambiguous citations before writes and refuse the batch with actionable candidate IDs."
  "2026-10-23T07:24:01.857Z",codex-agent,"Implementation: strong ownership matching stays first; exact qualified title/description/body citations fall back to a single existing item. All imports now prepare identities before writes, and ambiguous citations expose candidate IDs plus an exact tagging remedy. Adoption retains local tags and reports a separate count; provider-owned records retain link-only behavior. New tests use real trackers with a PATH containing node and the pinned pm CLI but no git, plus real git trackers for write-gate acceptance."
  "2026-10-23T07:27:45.693Z",codex-agent,"New citation suite: 13/13 passed, including plain/atomic adoption in non-git trackers, write-gate acceptance, retry identity, ambiguity refusal, punctuation, repo/number boundaries, structured ownership precedence and provider link-only preservation. Live pm-review main aa16d855df1f7b74afd3453617f77e92c44d493e already tags pm-review-withdrawn-lineage for issue 30, so an untouched current-main copy correctly plans update rather than adopt. Preserve this current-state result and locate the pre-tag historical tracker for a separate adoption replay. SDK reads may create runtime caches; verify original tracked file bytes independently."
  "2026-10-23T07:36:10.754Z",codex-agent,"Public dry-run evidence: current pm-review main aa16d855df1f7b74afd3453617f77e92c44d493e issue 30 plans 0 creates, 1 update, 0 adopts because PR 33 already added provenance. Actual pre-tag snapshot f72250e4c5ee8dfafaf57ee8afe20ddd3cbc993e plans 0 creates, 0 updates, 1 adopt into pm-review-withdrawn-lineage; gate new_entries=0. Current pm-context main 8d9576778a3609f156e9444ed659ca7c2e2aa9e7 plans 5 issues: 2 creates, 3 updates, 0 adopts, 0 skips, not truncated. All three are plain-directory archive copies. SHA-256 comparisons verify 106/106, 106/106 and 181/181 original files unchanged. Detailed receipts are in docs/cited-issue-adoption-validation.md."
