  "2026-10-23T07:42:06.837Z",codex-agent,"Mandatory linked verification completed: pm test pm-github-cited-issue-adoption --run --progress passed its one linked command, node --test test/cited-issue-adoption.test.ts (14 tests pass, zero failures/skips). Public tracker dry runs and behavioral revert evidence are complete. The ready-for-review PR will use CI npm run release:check and bun run release:check, unchanged thresholds, as full release-gate evidence; the final report will link the exact-head run and its counts. No merge or release is authorized."
  "2026-10-23T07:46:57.681Z",codex-agent,"Broader local regressions found a legacy plain-import assertion that expected an earlier issue to be written before a later structured ownership conflict. Universal identity preplanning intentionally removes that partial-write boundary. Updated the regression to require the unchanged tracker in plain, gated and atomic modes; structured matching and precedence remain unchanged. No production-code change was required. PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/169."
  "2026-10-23T07:49:35.957Z",codex-agent,"Focused write-boundary regression passed: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"ambiguous later issue\" test/import-fidelity.test.ts — 3 tests pass, zero failures/skips (plain, gated, atomic). This updates the old partial-write expectation to the fail-closed preflight contract. The initial CI run still tests the prior assertion; the next pushed head will contain this test-only correction and tracker receipt."
  "2026-10-23T08:27:20.623Z",codex-agent,"Final exact-citation audit reproduced an additional boundary miss: Issue: followed immediately by the issue URL, Reference:owner/repo#N, and a sentence-ending question mark returned new instead of citation. These are qualified prose citations under the acceptance criteria. Adjusted only the regex punctuation boundaries; retained negative URL query/path and longer-number cases. Added the forms to the existing pure matching regression, so test counts stay unchanged. The final source head will receive a fresh full npm/Bun CI run."
  "2026-10-23T08:29:20.672Z",codex-agent,"Punctuation boundary verification: typecheck, test typecheck and targeted lint passed. Four pure matching checks passed with the fix. Isolated behavioral revert restored only citesIssue to the preceding implementation: 1 of 4 checks failed (3 passed), proving the expanded boundary cases detect this correction. The general adoption revert remains 10 failures / 4 passes when only matchImportedIssue is restored to base main. All mutations remain covered by the real-tracker suite and the fresh full CI run."
  "2026-10-23T08:50:08.005Z",codex-agent,"CI identified one remaining legacy matcher parity assertion: GitHub issue: immediately followed by a URL was expected to remain new. The declared-ownership parser remains unchanged, but the new exact-citation fallback correctly adopts that form. Scoped both parity-table invocations to explicit adoption opt-out, preserving the original ownership grammar contract; default colon-citation behavior remains asserted in the new adoption suite. This is a test-only correction. The failed job passed 1034/1035 tests and reported four 100 percent coverage dimensions over all 18 authored modules."
  "2026-10-23T08:51:27.741Z",codex-agent,"Focused verification passed after the parity correction: node --test test/import-regex.test.ts test/cited-issue-adoption.test.ts — 21/21 pass, zero failures/skips. The full regex file was rerun with an explicit default-citation assertion for GitHub issue:URL (citation, linkOnly=false): 7/7 pass. Test typecheck and targeted lint passed. Reviewed every matchImportedIssue test call; strong ownership tests now explicitly opt out only where they assert the legacy grammar. Production source remains unchanged from bbe5718."
  "2026-10-23T09:59:05.116Z",codex-agent,"Review follow-up on PR 169: broad citation matching could overwrite or reopen a related-only closed item, and selecting only one issue could adopt a multi-issue roadmap. Tighten the fallback to one distinct qualified issue across all prose fields and explicit fix/track intent or a title reference. Preserve established ownership matching, report rejected incidental candidates with IDs/reasons, and retain ambiguity refusal only for two eligible owners. Remote PR head was pulled first; merged the one newer main commit containing CodeQL action updates."
  "2026-10-23T10:14:59.028Z",codex-agent,"Review regressions: node --test test/cited-issue-adoption.test.ts test/import-regex.test.ts passed 28/28 with zero failures/skips. Both plain and atomic closed-related items remain byte-equivalent in SDK fields while an open GitHub issue imports separately; roadmaps are never adopted when either issue is selected alone or both are selected. Positive closing words/labels/title cases and ambiguity among eligible owners remain covered. Behavioral revert in an isolated source copy restored only citesIssue and matchImportedIssue from pre-review head 4220a37, leaving planner/receipt code and SDK persistence real: the closed-incidental pattern failed 2/2, and the roadmap-only pattern failed 2/2, both exit 1 with no skips. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint and docstrings passed; the additional sorted multi-candidate receipt assertion passed its targeted check."
  "2026-10-23T10:18:02.884Z",codex-agent,"Real-data revalidation after the ownership guards: actual pre-tag pm-review f72250e4c5ee8dfafaf57ee8afe20ddd3cbc993e still plans one adopt into pm-review-withdrawn-lineage, zero creates (Fix URL description plus Issue: URL body, one distinct issue). Fresh pm-review main e1fc83a81507ca6a91f1675b74863c050f1a89f1 plans one provenance update. Fresh public pm-context main 7d7479ae77c13d01c54b2b4560ad54091ffed788 plans five issues: two creates, three updates, zero adopts/skips. Original file hashes remain unchanged 106/106, 106/106 and 181/181. The mandatory linked adoption test run passed 21/21. Strict tracker health passed after merging main; no merge maintenance was needed. Updated README examples and the validation document describe eligibility, incidental receipts and both review revert proofs."
  "2026-10-23T11:04:06.852Z",codex-agent,"Second review follow-up on PR 169: the distinct-issue regex omitted a trailing-slash issue URL, allowing a two-reference item to transfer ownership. The remote branch was pulled first and was unchanged. Replace this counting grammar with one parser used for intent and distinct identities, covering qualified shorthand, repository-hinted bare numbers, issue/PR URLs with trailing slash, fragments, query strings and prose punctuation. Add a property-style second-reference matrix and a real non-git persistence regression, then record a behavioral revert and fresh exact-head npm/Bun CI evidence."
  "2026-10-23T11:10:14.740Z",codex-agent,"The shared parser now normalizes issue/PR URL identities including trailing slash, query strings, comment fragments and Markdown punctuation. Repository-hinted bare references count toward additional targets but bare numbers and PR links alone cannot establish issue ownership. The property matrix checks 8925 second-reference combinations across all three fields plus 51 positive controls. Plain/atomic real non-git tracker regressions preserve the entire roadmap projection while creating the issue item. Combined adoption/regex suite passed 32/32 before the additional adjacent-Markdown boundary case, which also passes. Behavioral revert restored only citesIssue from cce11c4, retaining the new parser, receipts and real persistence: the property test plus both trailing-slash persistence tests fail (3 failures, 0 passes/skips, exit 1). Fixed cases pass. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings and zero-duplication checks passed."
  "2026-10-23T11:14:34.439Z",codex-agent,"Merged the newly advanced main toolchain update in 92f595e and installed its existing dependency pins (CLI, pm-ops and pm-changelog 2026.10.20). Reverified against those pins: mandatory linked adoption suite 25/25, regex suite 7/7, typecheck, test typecheck, build, lint, docstrings, zero duplication and strict tracker health pass. The current parser property matrix covers 8925 second-reference combinations plus 51 positive controls. The three-test behavioral revert was repeated against the updated toolchain and still fails 3/3 with zero passes/skips. Scoped coverage inspection found no uncovered branches in the new parser. The updated README and validation document explain the reference grammar and proof. Full unchanged-threshold npm/Bun release evidence will come from CI at the pushed correction head; no merge or release is authorized."
  "2026-10-23T11:43:37.620Z",codex-agent,"Exact-head CodeQL found a further issue in the shared parser: trimming punctuation with an unanchored suffix regex can backtrack quadratically on hostile URL text. The npm/Bun release phases pass, but this independent finding is valid. Replace that trim with the existing backwards scanner, preserve the default structured-locator punctuation behavior, and extend the existing adversarial regex regression harness. No review replies will be posted. The corrected source head will receive fresh release and CodeQL evidence."
  "2026-10-23T11:46:42.028Z",codex-agent,"CodeQL correction uses the existing backwards punctuation scanner with a citation delimiter set, preserving the default structured-locator behavior. The new real-matcher performance regression uses 50000 exclamation marks followed by a non-punctuation sentinel. Fixed best-of-three local time is 0.172 ms, under the existing 50 ms bound. Isolated behavioral revert restored only citationReferences from ef325ba while retaining the configurable scanner and test: 1 failure, 0 passes/skips, exit 1 at 3670.058 ms. This complements the three-failure ownership revert. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, the property matrix and scanner parity pass. Full affected suites and fresh exact-head release/CodeQL checks will verify the final correction."
  "2026-10-23T11:48:41.158Z",codex-agent,"Final local checks after the CodeQL trim correction pass: PM-linked node --test test/cited-issue-adoption.test.ts (25/25) and node --test test/import-regex.test.ts (8/8), with zero failures/skips. The second command is now registered on this item and was run through pm test --only-last --run --progress. Typecheck, test typecheck, build, lint, docstrings, zero duplication, privacy and strict tracker health pass. Performance revert command node --test --test-name-pattern=\"citation URL punctuation trigger\" test/import-regex.test.ts fails 1/1 with only citationReferences from ef325ba restored; fixed best-of-three 0.172 ms versus reverted 3670.058 ms. The earlier three-failure ownership revert remains recorded. The next pushed source head requires fresh npm/Bun release and CodeQL success before handoff."
  "2026-10-23T12:25:44.341Z",codex-agent,"Third review follow-up on PR 169: Markdown emphasis can hide a second URL from the strict parser. The remote branch was pulled first and was unchanged. Replace strict-parser exclusion with a deliberately broad raw-text veto for issues/digits, pull/digits and hash-digits substrings in all three prose fields, independent of wrappers or trailing characters. Keep the strict parser and explicit intent for positive ownership, preserve prior safeguards, and add fixed Markdown cases plus a deterministic random-decoration property regression. Over-counting must refuse adoption and return candidate hints. Record a function-only revert proof, then require fresh exact-head release and CodeQL evidence without replying to review threads."
  "2026-10-23T12:38:07.314Z",codex-agent,"Raw exclusion regressions pass: 192 fixed decoration/field cases, 4096 seeded nested-Markdown samples across all three fields (12288 property cases), 36 deliberate over-count cases and four repeated-number controls. The earlier 8925-case matrix and all earlier inputs remain; three foreign/malformed URL expectations now refuse their literal hash-31 substrings under the new policy. Mandatory linked commands pass 30/30 adoption tests and 8/8 regex/performance tests. Function-only revert restored citesIssue from 56580ec while retaining the new raw scanner, strict parser, receipts and real persistence: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"raw exclusion\" test/cited-issue-adoption.test.ts fails 5/5, zero passes/skips, exit 1. Fixed cases pass. Read-only saved-snapshot replay with the new rule preserves pm-review pre-tag one-adopt and tagged one-update plans; the five pm-context issues remain two creates/three updates with three incidental hints. All 393 original files retain their hashes. Typecheck, test typecheck and lint pass."
  "2026-10-23T12:41:03.214Z",codex-agent,"Local verification is complete for the raw exclusion design: both linked commands pass 38 tests total, and typecheck, test typecheck, build, lint, docstrings, zero duplication, privacy and strict tracker health pass. Scoped coverage inspection found no uncovered branches in the new raw scanner. README and validation evidence now distinguish the broad negative veto from strict positive ownership and explain intentional over-counting. No dependency pins or coverage thresholds changed. The next pushed head requires fresh npm/Bun release gates and CodeQL; the final CI URLs and exact counts will be added to PR 169."
  "2026-10-23T13:19:12.986Z",codex-agent,"Fourth review follow-up: replace the number-only raw veto with conservative repository-and-number attribution. Preserve strict positive ownership and intent. Add decorated foreign same-number issue and PR regressions, seeded repository/number/decoration fuzzing, real no-git persistence, a function-only revert proof, public snapshot replays and exact-head npm/Bun CI gates."
  "2026-10-23T13:23:58.277Z",codex-agent,"Repository veto implementation preserves qualified repository/number pairs while consuming their embedded fallback once. Every foreign, different-number or UNKNOWN reference refuses adoption with a multiple_issues candidate hint. Bare hashes remain UNKNOWN because the item projection carries no verified owning repository, and the import argument or another citation cannot supply it. Strict positive parsing/intent and established ownership precedence are unchanged. Fixed tests include 144 foreign same-number decoration/field cases, 4096 seeded repository/number/nested-decoration samples checked in all three fields (12288 cases), and plain/atomic no-git imports that preserve a completed local item instead of reopening it. Earlier inputs remain, with five now-UNKNOWN expectations updated to refusal."
  "2026-10-23T13:23:58.822Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: in an isolated source copy restore only hasOtherCitationNumber and citesIssue from aa86b21, retaining current tests, strict parser, receipts and real SDK persistence. Command: node --test --test-name-pattern='repository veto' test/cited-issue-adoption.test.ts. Reverted: 5 failures, 0 passes, 0 skips, exit 1, including both exact-reproduction persistence tests and fixed/fuzz/UNKNOWN tests. Fixed linked commands: node --test test/cited-issue-adoption.test.ts passes 35/35 and node --test test/import-regex.test.ts passes 8/8, run through pm test --run --progress. No test skips or failures."
  "2026-10-23T13:23:59.592Z",codex-agent,"Real-data dry runs re-fetched live GitHub issue/timeline reads against the saved read-only public tracker snapshots. pm-review pre-tag f72250e4c5ee8dfafaf57ee8afe20ddd3cbc993e: 0 create, 0 update, 1 adopt into pm-review-withdrawn-lineage, 0 skip. Tagged pm-review snapshot e1fc83a81507ca6a91f1675b74863c050f1a89f1: 0 create, 1 update, 0 adopt, 0 skip. pm-context snapshot 7d7479ae77c13d01c54b2b4560ad54091ffed788, issues 154,153,136,53,81: 2 creates, 3 updates, 0 adopts/skips. Three candidate hints now use multiple_issues because raw unattributable references veto before intent. All 393/393 original tracker files retain identical SHA-256 hashes."
  "2026-10-23T13:25:00.390Z",codex-agent,"Local verification complete: targeted commands pass 35/35 and 8/8 with zero failures/skips, including the final qualified-repeat control. Typecheck, build:test, build, lint, docstring (17 files, 187 declarations), duplication (18 modules, zero duplicated lines), privacy, strict tracker health and diff checks pass. Scoped coverage preflight found no uncovered branches in the changed veto functions. README and validation evidence document conservative UNKNOWN handling, fixed/property counts, function-only revert proof and public replay. Releasing the claim while leaving the item in_progress for orchestrator verification. Full npm/Bun release-gate counts and run links will be reported on PR 169 at the final pushed head after completion."
  "2026-10-23T13:58:03.276Z",codex-agent,"Fifth review changes the design: adoption becomes explicit opt-in across CLI, SDK and reusable workflow. Default imports retain create behavior with read-only citation hints. Normalize encoded and formatted text before conservative exclusion and anchored positive ownership. Keep earlier reproductions, add encoded-reference and seeded encoding fuzz regressions, verify the pre-tag public case with explicit opt-in, record behavioral reverts, and use exact-head CI npm/Bun gates."
  "2026-10-23T14:20:47.429Z",codex-agent,"Fifth-round implementation: CLI --adopt-cited, SDK adoptCited true and reusable input adopt-cited true are required. Defaults are false and preserve creates with read-only candidate hints, including competing eligible owners. A pinned entities 8.1.0 runtime decoder handles the full named/numeric HTML table and nested percent bytes over at most eight passes, with NFKC and default-ignorable control removal. Anchored title/leading-description/body-label ownership is separate from conservative normalized source/destination/soft-line exclusion. Malformed bytes and exhausted normalization refuse adoption. Tag items gh:owner/repo#N at creation as primary prevention. Source and link labels are retained for exclusion so unwrapping cannot hide another issue. Existing structured matching is unchanged."
