  "2026-10-23T15:21:29.341Z",codex-agent,"Performance fix preserves all normalized views but scans equal views once, finds issue/hash markers before reading the adjacent repository, and skips only identity Unicode/Markdown/soft-break transforms after decoding. Node source selection via c8 passes52/52 with no uncovered new-helper branches. Native local Bun1.3.5 regex/performance suite passes8/8, ownership200000-space probe22.892ms against unchanged50ms. Typecheck, builds, lint, docstrings and zero duplication across18 modules pass. Source-copy revert restores only normalizeCitationText, citationDisplayText and inspectCitationReferences from51dea17: bun test --test-name-pattern=\\\"ownership whitespace trigger\\\" test/import-regex.test.ts fails the selected test at112.322ms,1 failure,0 passes,7 filtered,exit1. Current anchored checks, tests, adjacent-repository helper and SDK paths remain. CI pinned Bun1.3.14 must provide its own fresh pass. No limits were relaxed."
  "2026-10-23T15:22:57.445Z",codex-agent,"Final optimized-code replay confirms unchanged public results in both modes: pre-tag pm-review creates1 by default with adoption_disabled and adopts1 with explicit opt-in, tagged pm-review updates1 in both, pm-context creates2/updates3 in both, zero skips, all393 original files unchanged. Revert command: bun test --test-name-pattern='ownership whitespace trigger' test/import-regex.test.ts. Reverted three performance functions fail1 selected test at112.322ms with7 filtered; fixed native suite passes8/8 at22.892ms for that probe. Node c8 source selection passes52/52, no uncovered new-helper branches. Typecheck, builds, lint, docstrings, zero duplication, strict tracker health and diff checks pass. Release the claim, retain in_progress, push the final optimization and require fresh CI npm/Bun/native gates at the unchanged limits."
  "2026-10-23T15:44:53.218Z",claude-orchestrator,"CodeQL (js/polynomial-redos, import-fidelity.ts:185) flagged the issue-label URL tail regex: its optional query group and the [.)]* tail overlap. The tail (>, then . or ), then spaces/tabs) is now trimmed by hand and the remaining anchored pattern has no overlapping quantifiers. New test pins the tail grammar (9 accepted tails, 4 refused tails, 50k-')' hostile input). Adoption suite 45/45, typecheck and lint pass."
  "2026-10-23T15:53:40.243Z",claude-orchestrator,"Review round 6 (codex) BLOCK: with --adopt-cited, an untagged item whose description says 'Fixes acme/widgets#30' but whose github_url names issue 31 was adopted for #30, overwriting #31's identity. Fix: an item with structured ownership (GitHub issue URL in github_url/provenance/external links, github_number, provider provenance, or a native 'GitHub issue <url>' declaration) is never adopted from prose; it is reported as a citation candidate with reason structured_owner. Regression test fails on revert (0/1) and passes with the fix; adoption suite 46/46; typecheck, lint, docstring, build pass. README lists the new reason."
  "2026-10-23T15:58:46.327Z",claude-orchestrator,"Delta review (codex) BLOCK: hasStructuredOwnership missed the core external_ref field, so an untagged item with external_ref gh:acme/widgets#31 citing #30 could still be adopted. Any non-empty external_ref (gh:, linear:, jira:, ado: or other) now counts as structured ownership. Tests for gh: and linear: external_ref; the structured-ownership test fails on revert and passes with the fix; suite 46/46; typecheck and lint pass."
  "2026-10-23T16:07:35.434Z",claude-orchestrator,"Enumerating review (codex) BLOCK: source_owner missed. hasStructuredOwnership now mirrors every ownership source identity.ts recognizes: any filled github_* field (except github_link_only true), github_link_only false, core external_ref and source_owner, linear_/jira_/ado_ id/key/url/identifier fields, provider provenance, native 'GitHub issue <url>' declaration, GitHub issue URLs in provenance/external links. Tests cover source_owner, jira_issue_key, github_state and github_link_only false; suite 46/46; typecheck, lint, docstring pass."
  "2026-10-23T16:19:17.181Z",claude-orchestrator,"Round 9 review (codex) BLOCK: githuburl alias (accepted by the owner matcher) was not treated as ownership. The guard now treats any github-prefixed field (except github_link_only) as ownership, and the owner-link field pattern is one shared constant (OWNER_LINK_FIELD) used by both the owner matcher and the adoption guard so they cannot drift again. Test adds githuburl; suite 46/46; typecheck, lint, docstring pass."
  "2026-10-23T16:28:46.869Z",claude-orchestrator,"Round 10 review (codex) BLOCK: an uppercase GH:owner/repo#N tag (recognized by identity.ts) did not mark ownership because the adoption filter's provenance-tag parser is lowercase-only. The guard now treats any well-formed GitHub identity tag in any case (identity.ts grammar, /^gh:owner/repo#N$/i) as ownership; malformed gh: tags keep today's behaviour. Test adds GH:other/widgets#31; suite 46/46; typecheck, lint, docstring pass."
